  "didacticJudgement": "The five existing targets teach laboratory handling/safety, instruction-bound actual preparation, indicator classification and aqueous ion concepts along the unchanged prerequisite route already leading to the current pH atoms. Their explicit target placement repairs acquisition visibility. This is a chosen didactic route including practical preparation, not a claim that numerical pH alone logically requires laboratory work or that the primary mandates these five whole goals verbatim. Canonical requires and whole ordinary goal texts remain unchanged.",
  "sourceBoundary": "Shared strong-acid/base duties are not authority for whole weak-acid/base target adoption in GK. The retained GK-strong/LK-weak and whole-source/course HOLDs remain. SL uses actual main GK/LK documents; RP actual69 is distinguished from immutable old25.",
  "practicalBoundary": "135170 and d2 remain real performance goals where their whole bodies require practical work. The corrected P-1 has a supervised real option; P-2 is explicitly a bounded facilitator simulation. Supplied expected logs, successful model transitions and this review establish zero actual learner laboratory execution. No new P/E1/G1 authority is inferred.",
  "HumanApproval": false,
  "HumanTrial": false
}
